      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure if retry really make sense here. Theorically, this TimerFdUtils.setExpirationTime() should never fails. Based on https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/timerfd_create.2.html\n\n```\n    timerfd_settime() and timerfd_gettime() can fail with the\n       following errors:\n\n       EBADF  fd is not a valid file descriptor.\n\n       EFAULT new_value, old_value, or curr_value is not a valid\n              pointer.\n\n       EINVAL fd is not a valid timerfd file descriptor.\n\n       timerfd_settime() can also fail with the following errors:\n\n       ECANCELED\n              See NOTES.\n\n       EINVAL new_value is not properly initialized (one of the tv_nsec\n              falls outside the range zero to 999,999,999).\n\n       EINVAL flags is invalid.\n```\n\n@reminv@google.com, do you have suggestion here.",
